  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape in late July 2026 is at a structural inflection point. The release of the 600-page CLARITY Act draft represents a critical shift from legislative uncertainty to formal federal oversight, setting a high bar for deterministic execution environments. While Bitcoin ETFs have faced a period of volatility and net outflow, institutional focus has decisively pivoted toward Bitcoin as a foundational treasury asset rather than a mere speculative instrument. Simultaneously, the DeFi sector is undergoing a necessary evolution; native, non-custodial cross-chain liquidity solutions are replacing legacy bridge architectures, effectively mitigating the systemic risks that have historically plagued the sector. The Clarity language continues to gain institutional favor, uniquely positioned to meet the deterministic security requirements prioritized by the new legislative framework, effectively challenging the EVM's dominance in high-stakes financial applications.",
